# queen-trap-fix.patch — ENGINE-5 fix (v2: qsearch + RFP guard + regression tests)
#
# Defect (benches/diagnostics/ 2026-11-27): quiet-reply queen traps are
# invisible to the search. The queen's own flight moves are quiet, so the
# capture-only qsearch never sees the queen captured at a flight square; stand
# pat keeps the static score (queen counted as alive) even while it is attacked;
# and reverse futility at depth <= 3 can seal the node entirely before any
# defence is searched. Against ENGINE-4 the trap suite shows 28 queen falls /
# 13 provable traps / 13 cases (9 decisive losses: 3 vs wowl-1.3.7 in both
# arms, 1 vs topple-0.1.1, 2 vs akimbo-0.1.1, 1 vs topple-0.2.1 in each arm).
#
# Fix contract (mission 2026-11-27, implemented here in full):
#   1. quiesce_core: when the mover has an attacked queen, (a) keep the FULL
#      legal move list (queen flights included) instead of captures-only,
#      (b) disable stand pat — "doing nothing" there loses the queen on the
#      opponent's next capture — which also disables delta pruning for the
#      node (delta only guards the stand-pat path).
#   2. search(): reverse futility pruning gets an explicit guard — one queen
#      scan plus at most two is_attacked probes, only at RFP-eligible nodes
#      (depth <= 3, non-PV, not in check) — and is skipped when the mover's
#      queen is attacked.
#   3. Pruning audit (AGENTS_LOG.md, 2026-11-27): futility's only return path
#      descends through quiesce_with_moves (the fixed quiesce), so futility
#      needs no separate guard; null-move pruning is direction-safe (after the
#      pass the opponent's queen capture is a capture and is searched); TT
#      cutoffs are safe once all nodes store fixed values. RFP was the one
#      unguarded return and is fixed here.
#   4. Full regression module queen_trap_tests (13 tests): the 7 avoidable needle trap
#      FENs plus the 6 broad/lost cases from trap_cases.json, stand-pat blindness on a real post-reply
#      fixture plus its color mirror, RFP sealing guard (and RFP preserved
#      without an attacked queen), multi-queen and one-attacked-of-many scans,
#      terminal states (mate, stalemate, insufficient, fifty-move), endgame
#      queen-preservation, quiet stand-pat behaviour preserved, in-check
#      legality, and strict searchmoves under the widened qsearch list.
#
# Apply on top of target cb7242cbb9a88a17e9c1a2b11437a507733e46eb (ENGINE-4).
